WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:05.520
Fact: Many of the best films from the last
decade also featured some of the best movie

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:07.000
villains we've ever seen.

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.220
From insidious music teachers to scheming
lovers, here are some of the biggest, meanest,

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.140
and most devious bad guys from the last decade.

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:18.240
Beware, there are major spoilers ahead!

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:23.520
Black Panther remains one of the best and
most important films in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.640
Universe, and the film's villain is easily
one of its most compelling elements.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.740
We're given quite the explosive introduction
to Erik "Killmonger" Stevens, played brilliantly

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:34.160
by Michael B. Jordan.

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.620
At the start of the film, we watch him pull
off one seriously epic museum heist.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:44.460
A military veteran who bears scars on his
body for each one of his kills, Killmonger

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:49.500
is undeniably one of the MCU's most fascinating
characters, and his motivations make a whole

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.220
lot of sense: He's out for revenge after his
father's murder at the hands of his own brother.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.540
Killmonger wants to use Wakanda's considerable
resources to liberate black people all over

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:00.780
the world from oppression.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:05.420
But he commits so many despicable and callous
acts through the film, it can be hard to see

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:06.920
him as a sympathetic character.

00:01:07.569 --> 00:01:12.759
There's no two ways about it: Jordan's masterful
performance easily cements Killmonger as one

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:15.420
of the most interesting villains of the last
decade.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:21.400
"You know, where I'm from, when black folks
started revolutions, they never had the firepower."

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:28.479
Not far into Jordan Peele's directorial debut,
Get Out, we meet Chris Washington and Rose

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:33.020
Armitage...a seemingly well-adjusted couple
played to perfection by Daniel Kaluuya and

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.080
Allison Williams.

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:38.400
At the start of the film, they're bracing
themselves for a weekend visit to Rose's parents'

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:42.180
house, a sprawling estate with no shortage
of creepy goings-on.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.160
Chris is initially quite nervous about meeting
Rose's family, but Rose doesn't appear worried

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.100
in the slightest.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:49.740
"Do they know I'm black?"

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:53.320
"No.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:56.700
Should they?"

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:02.520
Following an unnerving near-miss with a wayward
deer, their visit seems to go just fine at

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:07.360
first…although perhaps the conversations
are a little bit stilted and awkward at times.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:11.240
Of course, things eventually take a turn for
the decidedly sinister.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.960
Soon enough, Chris is getting seriously freaked
out by all the bizarro things happening at

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.240
the Armitage house, and he eventually tells
Rose that he wants to leave.

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:26.260
Rose seems to acquiesce...but just as it looks
like he's about to actually escape the estate,

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:31.560
the story throws another curveball our way:
Rose refuses to give up the keys.

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:34.319
She's decidedly not on Chris's side.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.220
And in a flash, she's gone from the girl next
door to one of the decade's most insidious

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:39.720
villains.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.600
Sometimes great movie villains are seemingly
normal people who nevertheless want to ruin

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:46.100
lives.

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:51.240
A perfect example is the character of Terence
Fletcher in Whiplash, masterfully portrayed

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.400
by J.K. Simmons.

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:53.460
"Look at me."

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.080
"One, two, three, four...One, two, three,
four…"

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.920
"Now, was I rushing?"

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.360
He's a conductor and teacher at the fictional,
prestigious Shaffer Conservatory.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:09.659
A devoted perfectionist and flat-out abusive
instructor, Fletcher singles out a student

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:11.940
named Andrew, played by Miles Teller.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:16.499
He's a young drummer in his first year at
the academy, and Fletcher goes to great ends

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.220
to make his life a living hell.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:23.110
As the two battle it out over Andrew's spot
in the band, some troubling information comes

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.520
to light about Fletcher.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:30.379
After Andrew testifies against Fletcher in
court, the twisted teacher intentionally sabotages

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.580
his young student during a pivotal performance.

00:03:33.430 --> 00:03:37.260
Simmons won a well-deserved Academy Award
for the role, and gives one of the defining

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.720
performances of his long and storied career.

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.760
Fletcher isn't a supervillain, but he's definitely
a monster.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:47.860
In fact, he's one of the scariest film characters
in recent memory.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.640
There's simply no way to sympathize with this
guy.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:56.840
No, he might not possess the raw, brutish
power of a villain like Thanos, but Loki certainly

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.520
corners the market on style and panache.

00:03:59.989 --> 00:04:04.700
This "god of mischief" has made memorable
appearances in more than a few MCU films,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.439
including the Thor movies and the Avengers
installments.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.280
Beyond that, the character will be getting
his very own namesake show on Disney+, and

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:16.440
it's expected to premiere on the streaming
service sometime in Spring 2021.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.800
Nevermind the fact that Loki is supposed to
be evil.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:24.520
He's become one of the most beloved characters
in the entire Marvel cinematic universe.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:29.580
The fact that audiences are basically rooting
for him has everything to do with Tom Hiddleston's

00:04:29.590 --> 00:04:32.500
rakish, undeniably charming performance.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:36.970
In fact, it seems like fans are willing to
overlook some of the character's worst trespasses

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:40.220
simply because they love Hiddleston's performance
so much.

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:42.940
"I guess I'll just have to go it alone.

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:45.560
Like I've always done."

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:50.660
In fact, that's a large part of what makes
Loki such a great villain: Even when he's

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.700
conspiring against Thor and the other good
guys, he still somehow manages to win us over

00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.200
somehow.

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.480
Well played, Loki.

00:04:57.780 --> 00:04:58.540
Well played.

00:04:59.420 --> 00:05:05.100
In Quentin Tarantino's 2012 Western Django
Unchained, Leonardo DiCaprio plays the film's

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.140
central villain, Calvin Candie.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.960
He's a brutal plantation owner with a serious
taste for violence…and he gets his kicks

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:15.360
by forcing slaves to fight to the death right
in front of him.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.860
To make matters worse, Candie owns Broomhilda,
played by Kerry Washington.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:24.180
She's the wife of the titular bounty hunter,
Django, portrayed by Jamie Foxx.

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:29.720
Candie is quite unwilling to let Broomhilda
go .In the hopes of rescuing her, Django hatches

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:30.460
a plan.

00:05:30.760 --> 00:05:35.800
Along with his traveling companion Dr. King
Shultz, played by Christoph Waltz, he manages

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.640
to infiltrate Candie's plantation.

00:05:38.220 --> 00:05:42.940
"I do believe you were just getting ready
to make me a proposition to buy Broomhilde.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.140
Am I right?"

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.220
Their plan, of course, goes horribly awry.

00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:52.220
DiCaprio's performance as Candie is totally
unforgettable, from start to finish.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:53.880
And what a finish it is.

00:05:54.680 --> 00:06:00.280
Mad Max: Fury Road captivated critics and
fans alike, earning ten Academy Award nominations

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.600
and ultimately raking in six wins.

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:07.470
Widely considered one of the best action films
ever made, Fury Road masterfully combines

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:10.260
heart-stopping action with an enthralling
narrative.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:15.409
The post-apocalyptic tale also features a
perfectly horrendous villain in the form of

00:06:15.409 --> 00:06:19.500
Immortan Joe, played by Australian actor Hugh
Keays-Byrne.

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:25.120
"We send off my War Rig to bring back gasoline
from Gas Town."

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.120
This creepy, barely-alive cult leader heads
an army that's fond of capturing healthy people,

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:33.680
to subsequently use for blood and breeding.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:40.440
At once entirely frail and incredibly intimidating,
Immortan Joe is a tyrannical dictator and,

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.640
it must be said, a really impressive driver.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.380
Not a good person, though.

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:49.960
Crafting a villain as iconic as Darth Vader
is certainly a tall order.

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:55.400
And while his shadow still looms over the
entire franchise, J.J. Abrams and Rian Johnson

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.920
managed to create an entirely new kind of
villain for the series.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:04.800
Audiences were first introduced to Kylo Ren
in the 2015 film Star Wars: The Force Awakens…and

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.120
he's portrayed marvellously by Adam Driver.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:11.780
An operative of the sinister First Order,
he didn't start out as a bad guy.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:16.760
In fact, he once trained as a Jedi under Luke
Skywalker himself…but he was ultimately

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:18.420
tempted by the Dark Side.

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.820
It happens.

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:26.060
Aided by Driver's explosive, thoughtful performance,
Kylo Ren is a multi-layered and complex villain.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:28.940
He's also a rather petulant one, too.

00:07:29.200 --> 00:07:33.340
He might be the powerful leader of the First
Order, but he still succumbs to the occasional

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:37.780
temper tantrum, which makes the character
feel all-too human at times.

00:07:37.980 --> 00:07:41.020
"I'll destroy her and you.

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.060
And all of it."

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:48.760
It's always a smart move to bring in a celebrated
actor to play a vicious and unapologetically

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:50.040
campy antagonist.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:55.539
And director Taika Waititi did just that by
casting Academy Award-winner Cate Blanchett

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.540
as the villain in Thor: Ragnarok.

00:07:57.760 --> 00:08:03.160
Thor faces a number of obstacles throughout
the film…but his biggest one is surely Hela,

00:08:03.160 --> 00:08:04.220
the goddess of death.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:09.120
Blanchett is clearly having a blast playing
the character, vamping up a storm even as

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:11.260
she doles out death blows by the bucketful.

00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:12.700
"Kneel."

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:13.960
"I beg your pardon?"

00:08:18.980 --> 00:08:19.660
"Kneel."

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.920
It's certainly a relief when Hela is defeated,
but it's also disappointing that Blanchett

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:27.660
likely won't be back for future Thor installments.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:33.140
Sometimes, a villain is hiding right there
in plain sight, taunting us all the while.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:38.020
And when this formidable foe finally reveals
their true identity, audiences are treated

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.100
to one seriously epic twist.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:44.360
The 2017 blockbuster Wonder Woman is a perfect
example of this.

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:49.100
As it turns out, Ares the god of war is very
much responsible for much of the film's mayhem,

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:54.720
and seeing as he's Diana's half-brother, he's
been right under her nose the entire time.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.660
"Only a god can kill another god."

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:03.260
Played by the always-mesmerizing David Thewlis,
Sir Patrick Morgan is initially introduced

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:05.300
to us as an advocate for peace.

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:10.060
But no, he's actually Ares in disguise…and
peaceful he is not.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:15.340
In the film's climax, he sheds his human persona
to go up against Diana once and for all.

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:21.900
Ultimately, Ares' two radically different
personas, not to mention Thewlis' convincing,

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.850
wildly entertaining performance, makes him
one of the last decade's most memorable movie

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:26.340
villains.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:31.000
It should go without saying that you simply
can't have a list of great villains without

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.120
including Thanos.

00:09:32.580 --> 00:09:37.460
As you're no doubt well aware, he's the resident
"big bad" throughout multiple phases of the

00:09:37.460 --> 00:09:39.920
Marvel Cinematic Universe, and for very good
reason.

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:45.750
Josh Brolin officially took on the role in
2014's Guardians of the Galaxy…and right

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.100
from the start, he makes the character his
own.

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:53.020
Thanos eventually decides that he should help
out the universe by cutting its population

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:57.850
in half by any means necessary, a belief instilled
in him after the people of his home planet

00:09:57.850 --> 00:10:00.180
Titan go extinct thanks to overpopulation.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:05.340
"Little one, it's a simple calculus: This
universe is finite.

00:10:05.340 --> 00:10:06.520
Its resources, finite."

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:11.480
Throughout several MCU films, Thanos spends
his time assembling the six Infinity Stones

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:14.120
to place them in the legendary Infinity Gauntlet.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:19.970
In Avengers: Infinity War, he finally achieves
his goal and "snaps" half of the world's living

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:21.720
beings out of existence.

00:10:21.900 --> 00:10:25.720
Nevertheless, he ultimately meets his crushing
defeat in Avengers: Endgame.

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:30.300
Without a doubt, Thanos ranks among the last
decade's greatest villains.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:35.150
He's cold-blooded, single-minded, and willing
to do whatever it takes to achieve his goal:

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:38.160
Namely, kill half the population of the universe.

00:10:38.980 --> 00:10:41.740
Gone Girl starts out with a rather familiar
narrative.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:47.370
Adapted by author Gillian Flynn from her insanely
readable novel, the film tells the story of

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.600
a young woman named Amy Dunne, played by Rosamund
Pike.

00:10:51.120 --> 00:10:54.980
She's apparently gone missing on the morning
of her fifth wedding anniversary.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:59.850
Unsurprisingly, her detached husband Nick,
played by Ben Affleck, quickly becomes the

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.600
main suspect in the apparent crime.

00:11:01.940 --> 00:11:07.120
Directed by David Fincher, Gone Girl incorporates
clever, dream-like flashbacks to let us see

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:10.880
how Nick and Amy's fairytale romance has steadily
turned sour.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.940
Halfway through the film, we make a startling
discovery: Nick is actually being framed by

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:16.460
Amy.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:21.800
After she discovers that he has been cheating
on her, she goes full-fledged diabolical and

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:23.280
totally fakes her kidnapping.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:27.880
She even plans to take her own life just so
she can pin her death on Nick.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:29.580
Talk about holding a grudge.

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:33.900
But then she eventually changes her mind and
decides she's going to try holding onto her

00:11:33.980 --> 00:11:36.520
husband, once and for all this time.

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:41.020
Throughout the film, it becomes all too clear
that Amy will stop at nothing to achieve her

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:42.180
infernal ends.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:47.640
She's even willing to murder her loyal childhood
love Desi, played by Neil Patrick Harris.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:53.060
And ultimately, she wins this insidious game:
She completely traps Nick, and the two start

00:11:53.060 --> 00:11:54.670
preparing to have a child together.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:58.760
As far as Nick is concerned, that's almost
certainly a fate worse than death.

